  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In view of the recent ratification of the MLC, 2006 and the reporting obligations of the country in 2021 (first report), two Government officials also participated in the Online Training Course on reporting on the MLC, 2006. Capacity-building measures continue to be needed in relation to the MLC, 2006. 
Number of member States with tripartite mechanisms enabling constituents to effectively engage in the implementation of international labour standards at the national level, including reporting to the supervisory bodies
&#x2022;	A training workshop on ILS and the ILO supervisory system is very much needed, this would be an opportunity to move towards the ratification of C144 and establish a tripartite mechanism on ILS, needs: about 20,00 USD (to be considered by the new Standards Specialist in 2024).
This CPO is in line with the Sustainable Development Agenda 2030 and will primarily contribute to assisting The Gambia to achieve Goal 8: Decent Work and Economic Growth, with a particular focus on targets 8.5, 8.7 and 8.8. The project will also contribute to Goal 5 (targets 5.1, 5.2, 5.4, 5.a, 5.c); Goal 10 (targets 10.2, 10.3, 10.4) and Goal 16 (16.2, 16.3, 16.7, 16.b).</narrative>
  </description>
